I have everything needed. Here is my report.

## Summary

This is a **Spring PetClinic REST** app converted to **OfficeFloor function injection**. Build system is **Maven** (`pom.xml`, `./mvnw` wrapper). All the household / duplicate / membership logic lives in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/` as small single-purpose helper classes, wired into the create/read owner flows.

---

## 1 & 2. Files and relevant code

### `HouseholdId` — generates/assigns the household identifier
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdId.java`

```java
public final class HouseholdId {
    private HouseholdId() {}

    public static String of(Owner owner) {
        String seed = key(owner.getLastName()) + "\n" + key(owner.getAddress());
        try {
            byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
                    .digest(seed.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(16);
            for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
                sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i]));
            }
            return sb.toString();
        }
        catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(e);
        }
    }

    private static String key(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```
Note the Javadoc says a household is "the set of owners with the same last name at the same **address**" — the hash seed is `lastName + "\n" + address`.

### `Household` — counts household size (NOTE: appears unused)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Household.java`

```java
public final class Household {
    private Household() {}

    public static int size(Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String householdId = HouseholdId.of(owner);
        return (int) ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .filter(other -> HouseholdId.of(other).equals(householdId))
                .count();
    }
}
```
I searched the whole `src` tree: **`Household.size(...)` has no callers.** It is currently dead code — household size does **not** feed into anything today (see item 5).

### `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique` — the `sharesHousehold` opt-in / household duplicate block
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`

```java
public class EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val Boolean sharesHousehold, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(sharesHousehold)) {
            return;
        }
        String lastName = key(owner.getLastName());
        String address = key(owner.getAddress());
        boolean clash = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .anyMatch(other -> key(other.getLastName()).equals(lastName)
                        && key(other.getAddress()).equals(address));
        if (clash) {
            throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(
                    "An owner with the same last name and address already exists");
        }
    }

    private static String key(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```

### `MembershipLevel` — computes membership level
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/MembershipLevel.java`

```java
public final class MembershipLevel {
    private MembershipLevel() {}

    public static int of(Owner owner, int namesakeCount) {
        int level = 1;
        if (owner.getEmail() != null) {
            level++;
        }
        if (namesakeCount == 0) {
            level++;
        }
        return Math.min(level, 3);
    }
}
```

### `IdentityKey` — the single value all hard duplicate detection is based on
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/IdentityKey.java`

```java
public final class IdentityKey {
    private IdentityKey() {}

    public static String of(Owner owner) {
        String telephone = owner.getTelephone() == null ? "" : owner.getTelephone();
        String email = owner.getEmail() == null ? "" : owner.getEmail();
        return telephone + "|" + email + "|" + HouseholdId.of(owner);
    }
}
```

### `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique` — the hard duplicate check
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique.java`

```java
public class EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateIdentityException {
        String identityKey = IdentityKey.of(owner);
        boolean taken = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .anyMatch(other -> identityKey.equals(IdentityKey.of(other)));
        if (taken) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException("An owner with the same identity already exists");
        }
    }
}
```

### `PossibleDuplicate` — soft duplicate detection (surfaced on the DTO)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/PossibleDuplicate.java`

```java
public final class PossibleDuplicate {
    private PossibleDuplicate() {}

    public static Integer of(Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
        if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
            return null;
        }
        return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .filter(other -> other.getId() != null && !other.getId().equals(owner.getId()))
                .filter(other -> postcode.equals(other.getPostcode()))
                .filter(other -> other.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName()))
                .filter(other -> !owner.getTelephone().equals(other.getTelephone()))
                .map(Owner::getId)
                .min(Integer::compareTo)
                .orElse(null);
    }
}
```

### `Namesakes` — feeds MembershipLevel
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Namesakes.java`

```java
public final class Namesakes {
    private Namesakes() {}

    public static int countBefore(Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        Integer id = owner.getId();
        if (id == null) {
            return 0;
        }
        return (int) ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .filter(other -> other.getId() != null && other.getId() < id)
                .filter(other -> other.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName()))
                .filter(other -> other.getFirstName().equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getFirstName()))
                .count();
    }
}
```

### `BuildOwner` — reads `sharesHousehold` off the request
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java` (relevant tail):
```java
public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built,
        Out<Boolean> sharesHousehold) throws ... {
    ...
    built.set(owner);
    sharesHousehold.set(Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold()));
}
```

### Escalation (409 for duplicate household)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler.java` — responds `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409).

Related sibling handlers also exist: `DuplicateIdentityException(+Handler)`, `DuplicateEmailException(+Handler)`, `DuplicateTelephoneException(+Handler)`.

### OwnerMapper — exposes `householdId`, `identityKey`, etc. on the DTO
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
@Mapping(target = "householdId", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.HouseholdId.of(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.IdentityKey.of(owner))")
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
```
(`membershipLevel`, `namesakeCount`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `contactPreference` are set imperatively in the Respond* functions, not the mapper.)

### DTO schema
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`
- `sharesHousehold` (input, `OwnerFields`, line ~2059): "When true, allow creating this owner even if another owner already has the same last name and address."
- `householdId` (output, line ~2118): "A stable identifier shared by owners at the same **address** with the same last name."
- `membershipLevel` (line ~2138): "1 to 3: starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when namesakeCount is 0, capped at 3."
- `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (lines ~2166-2178): "another owner shares this owner's last name and **postcode** but has a different telephone."

---

## 3. Where householdId is generated/assigned
`HouseholdId.of(Owner)` (SHA-256 of normalized `lastName + "\n" + address`, first 8 bytes → 16 hex chars). It is not stored on the entity; it is derived on read via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (`@Mapping householdId`) and consumed inside `IdentityKey.of` and `Household.size`.

## 4. Where duplicate detection happens
- **Hard duplicate (rejects create, 409):** `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique` via `IdentityKey.of` (full telephone|email|householdId match). `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique` is a separate hard block on lastName+address, bypassed by `sharesHousehold=true`. There are also standalone `EnsureOwnerEmailUnique` / `EnsureOwnerTelephoneUnique` in the same package.
- **Soft duplicate (informational flag on DTO):** `PossibleDuplicate.of` → set in `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` as `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.

## 5. Where membership level is computed / how household size feeds in
Computed in `MembershipLevel.of(owner, namesakeCount)`, called from `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated`. It currently uses **`namesakeCount`** (from `Namesakes.countBefore`) and email presence — **household size does NOT currently feed into membership level.** The `Household.size(...)` helper exists but has **no callers anywhere** in the codebase (confirmed via grep). If the task is to make household size drive membership level, `Household.size` is the ready-made but currently-unwired input.

## 6. Existing tests
Only one relevant test file:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`

```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId() throws Exception {
		String lastName = uniqueLastName();
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		a.put("lastName", lastName);
		a.put("postcode", "2000");
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", lastName);
		b.put("postcode", "2000");
		b.put("sharesHousehold", true); // same household -> bypass the duplicate block
		String ha = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(a)).get("householdId").asText();
		String hb = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(b)).get("householdId").asText();
		assertEquals(ha, hb);

		ObjectNode c = ownerNode(); // different lastName, same postcode
		c.put("postcode", "2000");
		String hc = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(c)).get("householdId").asText();
		assertNotEquals(ha, hc);
	}
}
```

Base/helpers: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` (helpers `ownerNode()`, `uniqueLastName()`, `uniqueAddress()` = `seq()+" Test Street"`, `createOwnerOk()`, `fetchOwner()`, `withPostcode()`, `structuredOwner()`).

**Important discrepancy to flag:** the test's comment and assertions describe householdId as "deterministic from (lastName, postcode)", and in the test owners `a` and `b` get the **same lastName but different addresses** (each `ownerNode()` calls `uniqueAddress()`), yet it asserts equal householdIds. But `HouseholdId.of` currently hashes **lastName + address**, so with differing addresses these would produce *different* hashes. So the current implementation (lastName+address) is inconsistent with what this test asserts (lastName+postcode). This test likely encodes a target contract the implementation does not yet satisfy — worth confirming against the intended change.

## 7. Build system & running tests
- **Maven**, with the wrapper `./mvnw` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`, `mvnw.cmd`) and `.mvn/`. `pom.xml` uses `spring-boot-maven-plugin`, `spring-boot-starter-test`, and OfficeFloor `woof_test`. No custom surefire/failsafe config (default Surefire).
- Run all tests: `./mvnw test` (from `/home/daniel/sandbox`).
- Single test class: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`
- Single method: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest#coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`
- Full verify/package: `./mvnw verify` / `./mvnw package`.

I did not modify anything.

